# what the daemon reads before a build starts. an allowlist rather than a list
# of exclusions, because `target/` here is hundreds of gigabytes and a context
# that picks it up by accident is a build nobody waits out.
#
# everything is out:
*
# and back in: exactly what `cargo build --example demo` opens.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src
!examples
# cargo will not parse a manifest whose [[test]] targets are missing, whatever
# it was asked to build
!tests
# the embedded ui, committed rather than built here; see the Dockerfile
!ui/dist
